UnitQueueLib::ProcessWithdrawals
├── when the queue is empty
│   ├── it should settle nothing
│   └── it should pass the counters through
└── given the queue is not empty
    ├── when the idle weight cannot cover the head exit
    │   ├── it should settle nothing
    │   └── it should leave the queue untouched
    └── given the queued exits are affordable
        ├── it should price each exit at shares times backing over supply
        ├── it should release exactly each entrys escrow and pair burn the holder
        ├── it should delete each settled entry
        ├── it should debit the backing and the pending shares
        ├── it should emit a WithdrawProcessed event per exit
        ├── when max entries is below the queue size
        │   └── it should settle only max entries in FIFO order
        ├── when a later exit is unaffordable
        │   └── it should stop the drain at the first unaffordable exit
        ├── given the relay is closed
        │   ├── it should burn each settled exits principal in full
        │   ├── it should skip the yield burn entirely
        │   └── it should settle the whole batch
        ├── when the destination is the mint sentinel
        │   └── it should route the weight to a freshly minted token
        ├── when the source stake is permanent
        │   ├── when the destination stake is also permanent
        │   │   └── it should route the weight to the named destination
        │   ├── when the destination stake is not permanent
        │   │   └── it should fall back to minting a fresh token
        │   └── when the surviving destination already holds stake
        │       └── it should emit the weight delivered above the previous stake
        ├── when the source stake is not permanent
        │   ├── when the destination stake is permanent
        │   │   └── it should route the weight to the named destination
        │   ├── when the destination unlock is not earlier than the source unlock
        │   │   └── it should route the weight to the named destination
        │   └── when the destination unlock is earlier than the source unlock
        │       └── it should fall back to minting a fresh token
        └── when the ratio carries across a batch
            └── it should price a known two exit example at the simulated ratios
